// P7 wave 2 package B3. THE NAMES OF EVERY WAY THE MAGMA WIRE ARM CAN DECLINE.
//
// A DECLINE IS NOT ALWAYS A SKIPPED DRAW. The SetupWireDraw / DispatchWireCompute rows are one
// per refused draw or dispatch; the Tex* / Shape* / Upload* rows are counted per texture SYNC,
// which the draw path reaches once per sampled texture and the descriptor resolver, framebuffer
// attachments, CopyTexSubImage, mipmap generation, CopyImageSubData and texture readback reach
// on their own (WireDeclineTally.h, above MGL_WIRE_DECLINE_AT).
//
// CONTRACT-P7 §0 rule I says a refusal on the wire arm is either a named decline or a named
// Fatal. Before B3 the draw path had a third shape the rule does not admit: a bare
// `return false` with no log, no counter and no census entry - roughly twenty of them in
// SetupWireDraw alone, plus the texture-sync chain behind PrepareWireTextureResources. A draw
// that took one of those exits left NO trace anywhere, which is precisely why the OpenRA
// device divergence survived four device windows with client and server logs that were
// LINE-IDENTICAL between a passing and a failing run.
//
// Each row below is one such exit. The name is what the decline logs and what the tally
// counts, so "which exit did this frame take" is answerable from a counter dump instead of
// from a bisect. Rows are append-only: the integration lane asserts specific counters moved.
//
// EVERY ROW HAS A SITE AND EVERY SITE HAS A LINE. A row with no site is a name that can never
// be counted - it reads as "this cannot happen here" when it only means "nobody wired it up" -
// and a site with no line puts the reader back on a bisect. Sites reached through a macro
// (MGL_WIRE_DECLINE_AT) get both at once; the few that use WireDeclineTally::Count directly do
// so ONLY because the statement above them already carries the same reason as an _ONCE log.
// scripts/ci/wire_declines_audit.py holds both halves.
//
// MGL_WIRE_DECLINE(Name)

// ---- SetupWireDraw, in statement order -------------------------------------------------
